<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ WINS TARIFF CUTS ON DAIRY INTO CHINA-SMITH.</title>
<headline>NZ WINS TARIFF CUTS ON DAIRY INTO CHINA-SMITH.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand International Trade Minister Lockwood Smith said on Wednesday he hoped major exporters such as the Dairy Board would gain substantially from lower tariffs on a range of products negotiated with China.</p>
<p>He said tariffs on butter and cheese would fall from 65 percent to 25 percent, from 35 percent to 25 percent on milk powder and from 30 percent to 20 percent on liquid milk as part of bilateral negotiations in Beijing related to China's accession to the World Trade Organisation (WTO).</p>
</text>
